From 7ea5d20cb7b6c1692dd910cf98e9a755a2b008d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicole Muzzin <nicks@fuckin.email>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 01:21:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] svg: inline targets of external-document <use
 href="file.svg#id">

GitLab (and many design systems) draw every icon as <svg><use href="/assets/icons.svg#name">.
The inline svg is rasterized from a standalone serialization that cannot fetch anything, so
these icons were empty.

The first serialization that meets such a reference starts a same-origin fetch of the
document (once per URL per document, like Chrome, which refuses cross-origin <use>), parses
it as image/svg+xml the way DOMParser does, and invalidates the waiting svgs when it
arrives. Later serializations clone the referenced element into the svg's <defs> under an id
unique to the serialization, since the page may define the same id itself, and rewrite the
use element's serialized href to point at the copy.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
